{"availability":"available","full":"systemsomicslab/MsdialWorkbench","name":"MsdialWorkbench","description":"Universal workbench incorporating msdial, msfinder, and mrmprobs","category":"Other","language":"C#","stars":123,"forks":42,"created":"2023-01-13T10:40:40Z","updated":"2026-10-12T01:54:05Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://systemsomicslab.github.io/compms/msdial/main.html","topics":[],"demo":"https://systemsomicslab.github.io/compms/msdial/main.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:59.980Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:59.980Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:59.980Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:42.932Z","stars":123,"forks":41},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.647Z","stars":123,"forks":41},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:27:59.980Z","stars":123,"forks":42}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The program supports data processings for any type of chromatography / scan type mass spectrometry data, and the assembly is licensed under the CC-BY 4.0.","The LBM (.LBM2) file contains the in silico MS/MS spectra of lipids. There are currently three files named with 'FiehnO (Oliver Fiehn laboratory)', 'AritaM (Makoto Arita laboratory)', and 'SaitoK (Kazuki Saito laboratory)'. These files contain the same MS/MS spectra information but have different predicted retention times which were optimized for the indivisual method. One of the '.LBM' files which contains lipid's in silico MS/MS should be also in the same folder as 'MSDIAL.exe' for Lipidomics project."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/systemsomicslab/MsdialWorkbench/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"f3a930b5c103456ad04c03b188e35fd89774144419efcbcc5b6e5ecf719137bc","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:43.076Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:45.787Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The program supports data processings for any type of chromatography / scan type mass spectrometry data, and the assembl